# BUGS

It only probes: the CSF firmware is read but not loaded, and nothing is drawn or computed on the GPU.
The power-up is the Sky1's alone.
`power DEVICE off` and `on` in devmgr's `ctl` (devmgr(8)) cut the GPU and bring it back, each time with a new host that probes it again.
The GPU's own MMU isn't set up, and its DMA, through the stub's BTI, would reach all of memory: nothing confines it once it is.
